{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PLAN CORRECTED after review-plan BLOCKED with three findings. All three were right, and TWO of them\ncorrected MY OWN audit — which is the useful part of this entry.\n\nBLOCK 1 (COH/E1) — the Scope section still said 'implement set_entity_property' while the Approach\nsection explicitly REJECTED the single-method fix and AC1 demanded all of them. An implementer reading\nScope alone would have done exactly the thing the plan argues against. My earlier edit updated\nContext/Approach/ACs and missed Scope. Fixed, and the stale counts elsewhere ('nine more', 'the core\ncalls fifteen', 'I found ten') are now consistent too.\n\nBLOCK 2 (E4) — I claimed a blanket 'no member may be absent, so no call site can fail with\nAttributeError'. Wrong for get_parent_map: fetcher.py:448 reads\n'if project_key and hasattr(client, \"get_parent_map\")', so its absence degrades to an empty parent\nmap rather than crashing. Verified by reading the line. It is still a real gap — DC silently loses\ninbound parent relationships — but it is a FUNCTIONAL gap needing a deliberate decision, not an\nAttributeError fix, and the plan now separates the two categories with its own AC.\n\nBLOCK 3 (G6) — the reviewer found delete_issue_link (dispatch_one.py:731), which my audit MISSED.\nDiagnosing why mattered more than adding it: my AST pattern matched only 'client.method(...)' CALL\nforms, but the reconciler routinely passes the method as a VALUE —\n'_call_with_retry(client.delete_issue_link, link_id)'. set_entity_property itself is called that way\nat dispatch_one.py:321 and I only caught it because it ALSO appears in call form at\nbinding_store.py:517. Pure luck.\n\nRe-ran the audit collecting EVERY attribute access on a client/transport receiver, not just calls.\nThat found delete_issue_link AND a second one nobody had spotted: set_parent (dispatch_one.py:544).\n\nCORRECTED FIGURES: the core reaches for 21 distinct transport members; TWELVE are absent from\nJiraDataCenterTransport (was 'ten'). Eleven are unguarded and would raise AttributeError; get_parent_map\nis the lone hasattr-guarded one. All twelve exist for Cloud.\n\nTHE LESSON, worth carrying: a static audit is only as good as its match pattern, and a narrow pattern\nfails SILENTLY — it returns a confident, wrong, smaller number. I had already published 'ten' as a\nmeasured fact before the reviewer disproved it. Measurement is not automatically evidence; the\nmeasuring instrument needs checking too."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785476496820227001,"uuid":"5def6987-73c1-4060-8717-0b56b44dbf82"}